[{:seon.task/name "the-status-reads-proof-facts"
  :seon.task/plan "Agreed tests-context 2026-11-14 (the owner's standing rule: a mechanism is kept once). A test's result is kept in five places (verdict files, .recent history, reads.edn, the :seon.test/* facts, data's :seon.proof/proof-fact); the Flow series writes only the proof-fact (seon.test-store/a-process-test-forks-the-running-runtime). Change: seon.ctx.status/verdicts (status.clj:131) and the ui and turn renders read a proof's verdict as the newest :seon.proof/proof-fact of its test, through data's pattern, in the landing after tests' writer; record-results!, proofs/result-tx and the :seon.test/status, digest and failures facts are deleted with it. What it needs from data's pattern [M, context]: (1) status, failures, ticks and bytes (:seon.proof/cost), and what replaces :seon.test/proved (read twice in render.ui); (2) one indexed read of the tests whose current verdict on the branch is not green (red, flaky, deferred), never a scan of proof history: an old red a green replaced does not count; (3) current means the verdict at the test's reach now, flaky being two statuses at one reads-digest. Owner: context; data shapes the pattern; tests writes the facts."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.test-store/a-process-test-forks-the-running-runtime"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.ctx.status-test/a-proofs-verdict-is-the-newest-proof-fact-at-its-reach}}

 {:seon.task/name "the-status-reads-mains-reds-as-the-judge-does"
